<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">31 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 31 August, from 1422 to 1997.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/england" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/england.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1422 CE <span class="tih-ago">604 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry V of England dies at Vincennes</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Henry V, victor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-agincourt">Agincourt</a> and heir to the French throne, died of dysentery aged 35. His nine-month-old son Henry VI inherited a dual monarchy that soon unravelled.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1886 CE <span class="tih-ago">140 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">An earthquake devastates Charleston, South Carolina</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A powerful earthquake struck Charleston, damaging most of its buildings and killing about 60 people. It remains the strongest recorded earthquake in the south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1888 CE <span class="tih-ago">138 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mary Ann Nichols is murdered in Whitechapel</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The body of Mary Ann Nichols was found in Buck's Row, the first of five victims generally attributed to 'Jack the Ripper'. The killer was never identified.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1939 CE <span class="tih-ago">87 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">SS men stage a fake Polish attack at Gleiwitz</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">SS operatives seized the German radio station at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gliwice">Gleiwitz</a> and broadcast an anti-German message, posing as Polish raiders. Hitler used such incidents to justify invading <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> the next morning.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1962 CE <span class="tih-ago">64 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Trinidad and Tobago becomes independent</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trinidad">Trinidad</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tobago">Tobago</a> gained independence from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eric-williams">Eric Williams</a> as prime minister. Oil and gas wealth made it one of the most prosperous nations in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1997 CE <span class="tih-ago">29 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Diana, Princess of Wales dies in a Paris car crash</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Diana was fatally injured when her car crashed in the Pont de l'Alma tunnel while pursued by photographers. Her death provoked an extraordinary outpouring of public grief in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and beyond.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li></ol>
